# M5 — Gateway topology endpoints

### `src/amr_dispatcher_tools/src/rest_gateway.cpp`
Router additions in `Dispatch` (exact match, `PathMatches`):
```cpp
GET  /api/v1/topology/overlay      -> HandleTopologyOverlay()
GET  /healthz                      -> (probe lane, M1.2 — not here)
POST /api/v1/topology/hot_update   -> HandleTopologyHotUpdate(req)
POST /api/v1/topology/preview      -> HandleTopologyHotUpdate(req, /*force_dry_run=*/true)
POST /api/v1/topology/block_edge   -> HandleTopologyBlockEdge(req)
POST /api/v1/topology/unblock_edge -> HandleTopologyBlockEdge(req, /*force_action=*/"unblock")
```
Handlers mirror `HandleForceClear` (`:652-695`): required fields (`operator_id`, `reason`, `confirm`, plus edge ids or `overlay_yaml`) → `400 invalid_request`; `wait_for_service(1s)` → `503 service_unavailable`; `fut.wait_for(topology_op_timeout_ms)` (default 10000, because a reroute of N vehicles is slow) → `504 timeout`; then map `error_code`:

| error_code | HTTP |
|---|---|
| `ok`, `no_change` | 200 (`"status":"ok"` / `"status":"noop"`) |
| `invalid_request`, `not_confirmed` | 400 |
| `map_hash_mismatch`, `would_disconnect_topology`, `edge_occupied_in_flight`, `would_strand_vehicles`, `lock_conflict`, `overlay_invalid` | 409 |
| `unknown_edge` | 404 |
| `catalog_unavailable` | 503 |
| `overlay_persist_failed`, `internal_error` | 500 |

Response body always includes `error_code`, `message`, `impacted_vehicles`, `impacted_missions`, `overlay_revision`, and for 409 on connectivity, `unreachable_nodes` — the console renders these verbatim.

`GET /api/v1/topology/overlay` → `GetTopologyOverlay(include_yaml=true)` (yaml only when `?yaml=1`), returns counts + revision + hashes + the yaml text; also caches the counts for the M2.4 gauges (single place, so `/metrics` and the console never disagree).

